<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστροφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρέφω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without turning round</i> or <i>away, fixed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					99
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφέρπειν ἄ.</span> go away
				<i>without turning back,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				490
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>without turning</i> or <i>twisting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				282d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>without strophe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Heph.
			</span></i><i>Poëm.</i><i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
